From: bakhodirovxz <bohodirovasadbek1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 02:25:27 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/22] xlsx: read shared formulas and filled-down runs as
 shared trees

The cells of an Excel shared formula (`<f t="shared" si=..>`) now hold shifted copies of the
master's tree instead of a re-printed, re-parsed formula each. Ordinary formulas that are the
formula above or to the left moved to their cell (most producers other than Excel write a
filled-down column that way) share its tree too: each is compared with `is_shifted_copy`, so a
run is only ever formed from formulas that are exactly copies, and a follower is not printed.

On a 10 MB generated workbook (432,120 formulas, written without shared formulas) the open peak
goes from 635 to 352 MB (40 MB workbook: 2,525 to 1,390 MB), with the evaluator unchanged and
every computed value identical.
